## 🔧 1 intro JSX & Babel

* JSX (JavaScript XML) is the syntax used in React to write HTML-like code in JavaScript.

  * **JSX allows you to write markup directly inside JavaScript**, making UI code easier to read and write.
* **JSX is not valid JavaScript**, so tools like **Babel** are used to convert (or transpile) it into regular JavaScript.

  * This conversion transforms JSX into `React.createElement` calls that browsers understand.
* You can see how JSX is compiled using the Babel REPL:
  👉 [http://babeljs.io/repl](http://babeljs.io/repl)

